A||||11||Jaei Sun||Headliner Fiberboard fix?||||1||
Z||000000||Jaei Sun||08-26-2001||12:30 AM||||Alright I just removed my Headliner out of my GT and noticed that it's broken in half in 2 locations.  It looks like they were done by the original person who took it out before me.  Trust me I took it out as easily as possible.  Now I want to fix these breaks what should I use?<P>I thought about using Fiberglass Resin in the break would that work or does a specific product exist for this?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-26-2001||12:35 AM||||1st, sweep off the board with a broom to remove all of the old glue and headliner material.  Then put the pieces back together with fiberglass mat and resin, then coat the entire board (both sides) with resin.  It'll come out fairly solid.  I just did mine (broken in 3 spots) and haven't had any trouble with it since.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jaei Sun||08-26-2001||12:47 AM||||Thanks a ton MonkeyMan!!!! I'm going to fix it now!!||||reg||14
