Z||000008||David Bartlett||08-27-2001||04:55 PM||||You can fix it with bondo (lightstraned) and drywall tape. It worked well for me.||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadaver||08-28-2001||12:54 AM||||bondo and drywall tape? No. It is made from compressed fiberglass so use 'glass resin and cloth.||||reg||1
Z||000010||84Bill||08-28-2001||12:55 PM||||Use thin CA glue. Its available at most hobby stores and it works great! Just put the t pieces together and shoot some CA in the crack. VIOLA! instant fix||||reg||14
Z||000011||cadaver||08-29-2001||12:19 AM||||I guess the CA glue. Cyano-acrylate. Or crazy glue/super glue. But I think it would make the joint really stiff and it would just crack next to the joint. I would much rather use 'glass resin on the whole thing and make it all strong not just parts or it.||||reg||1
